{{DISPLAYTITLE:Help:Saintapedia Graph}}

'''Saintapedia Graph''' turns [[mw:Extension:Cargo|Cargo]] query results into interactive [https://mermaid.js.org/ Mermaid] flowcharts — especially '''organization charts''' and '''funder → fundee''' (or any source → target) networks.

{{note|This page documents '''Saintapedia Graph 0.2.2''': hierarchy, edge, and dual-table modes, plus <code>style_by</code>, <code>subgraph_by</code>, and cycle warnings. Editor-facing messages are '''English only'''; other interface languages fall back to English.}}

== Requirements ==

* [[mw:Extension:Cargo|Extension:Cargo]] (required)
* Saintapedia Graph (this extension)
* MediaWiki 1.39+ / PHP 8.1+

'''You do ''not'' need Extension:Mermaid.''' Saintapedia Graph ships a bundled Mermaid library and renders diagrams itself.

== Quick start ==

=== 1. Declare Cargo tables ===

'''Organizations''' (hierarchy / org chart):

<pre>
{{#cargo_declare:_table=Organizations
|Name=String
|ParentOrg=Page
|Type=String
|Country=String
|Website=URL
}}
</pre>

'''Grants''' (edges / funding network):

<pre>
{{#cargo_declare:_table=Grants
|Funder=Page
|Recipient=Page
|Amount=Float
|Year=Integer
|Program=String
}}
</pre>

Store rows with <code>#cargo_store</code> (usually from a template), then create the tables at [[Special:CargoTables]] if needed.

=== 2. Draw an org chart ===

<pre>
{{#saintapedia_graph:
tables=Organizations
|fields=_pageName=Name,ParentOrg,Type,Country
|parent_field=ParentOrg
|node_id=Name
|style_by=Type
|subgraph_by=Country
|direction=TD
|clickable=yes
}}
</pre>

Edges are drawn '''parent → child''' (top-down reporting line). Or use <code><nowiki>{{Org chart|style=Type|subgraph=Country}}</nowiki></code>.

=== 3. Draw a funding network ===

Dual-table (organizations as nodes, grants as edges):

<pre>
{{#saintapedia_graph:
nodes_table=Organizations
|nodes_fields=_pageName=Name,Type,Country
|edges_table=Grants
|edges_fields=Funder,Recipient,Amount
|edges_where=Year>=2023
|node_id=_pageName
|node_label=Name
|source_field=Funder
|target_field=Recipient
|edge_label=Amount
|style_by=Type
|subgraph_by=Country
|direction=LR
|theme=forest
}}
</pre>

Or: <code><nowiki>{{Funding network|style=Type|subgraph=Country|edges_where=Year>=2023}}</nowiki></code>.

Single-table edge mode (no separate nodes query):

<pre>
{{#saintapedia_graph:
tables=Grants
|fields=Funder,Recipient,Amount,Year
|source_field=Funder
|target_field=Recipient
|edge_label=Amount
|direction=LR
|clickable=yes
|theme=forest
}}
</pre>

=== Live demo on this wiki ===

See [[Saintapedia Graph demo]] for seeded Organizations + Grants data.

== Relationship modes ==

You must choose '''one''' mode per diagram (mixing hierarchy and edge parameters is an error).

{| class="wikitable"
! Mode
! When to use
! Required parameters
! Edge direction
|-
| '''Hierarchy (parent)'''
| Org charts, subsidiaries, “reports to”
| <code>parent_field=…</code>
| Parent → child
|-
| '''Edge (source / target)'''
| Funding, partnerships, ownership links from one query
| <code>source_field=…</code> '''and''' <code>target_field=…</code>
| Source → target
|-
| '''Dual-table'''
| Nodes from one Cargo table, edges from another
| <code>nodes_table=…</code> '''and''' <code>edges_table=…</code> plus source/target fields
| Source → target
|}

Dual mode runs '''two''' Cargo queries and counts as two expensive parser functions.

Optional edge caption: <code>edge_label=Amount</code> (or any field).

=== Dual-mode identity ===

Edge endpoints (<code>Funder</code>, <code>Recipient</code>) are usually '''page titles'''. Prefer:

<pre>
|node_id=_pageName
|node_label=Name
</pre>

so edges match organization pages. If you use <code>node_id=Name</code>, '''Name must equal the page title'''.

== Parameters ==

=== Cargo query (same spirit as <code>#cargo_query</code>) ===

{| class="wikitable"
! Parameter
! Description
|-
| <code>tables</code> / <code>table</code>
| Required for hierarchy and edge modes. One or more Cargo tables (comma-separated).
|-
| <code>fields</code>
| Columns to select. The extension will add any fields it still needs for the diagram.
|-
| <code>where</code>
| Filter (Cargo/SQL-style conditions).
|-
| <code>join on</code>
| Join conditions when using multiple tables. Required if more than one table is listed in <code>tables=</code>.
|-
| <code>group by</code> / <code>having</code>
| Aggregation (same rules as Cargo).
|-
| <code>order by</code>
| Sort order.
|-
| <code>limit</code>
| Max rows (capped by site config, typically 1000).
|-
| <code>offset</code>
| Skip initial rows.
|}

=== Dual-table query ===

{| class="wikitable"
! Parameter
! Description
|-
| <code>nodes_table</code> / <code>edges_table</code>
| Required together. Two Cargo tables.
|-
| <code>nodes_fields</code> / <code>edges_fields</code>
| Columns for each query. Defaults add the fields the diagram still needs.
|-
| <code>nodes_where</code> / <code>edges_where</code>
| Per-query filters.
|-
| <code>nodes_join_on</code> / <code>edges_join_on</code>
| Per-query joins.
|-
| <code>nodes_order_by</code> / <code>edges_order_by</code>
| Per-query sort.
|}

=== Diagram ===

{| class="wikitable"
! Parameter
! Default
! Description
|-
| <code>direction</code>
| <code>TD</code>
| Layout: <code>TD</code> (top-down), <code>LR</code> (left-right), <code>BT</code>, <code>RL</code>
|-
| <code>node_id</code>
| <code>_pageName</code>
| Field that uniquely identifies a node
|-
| <code>node_label</code>
| same as <code>node_id</code>
| Text shown on the node
|-
| <code>page_field</code>
| hierarchy: <code>_pageName</code>; dual: <code>_pageName</code>; edge: ends themselves
| Wiki page title used for click links
|-
| <code>parent_field</code>
| —
| Hierarchy mode only
|-
| <code>source_field</code> / <code>target_field</code>
| —
| Edge and dual modes (both required)
|-
| <code>edge_label</code>
| —
| Optional edge caption field
|-
| <code>style_by</code>
| —
| Color nodes by this Cargo column (must be a real column)
|-
| <code>subgraph_by</code>
| —
| Group nodes by this Cargo column (must be a real column)
|-
| <code>link_style</code>
| <code>--></code>
| <code>--></code>, <code>-.-></code>, <code>==></code>, <code>---</code>, <code><--></code>
|-
| <code>clickable</code>
| <code>yes</code>
| <code>yes</code>/<code>no</code> — click node opens the wiki page
|-
| <code>theme</code>
| <code>default</code>
| Mermaid theme: <code>default</code>, <code>base</code>, <code>dark</code>, <code>forest</code>, <code>neutral</code>. Unknown values fall back to <code>default</code> and show a warning.
|-
| <code>warn_cycles</code>
| <code>yes</code>
| Warn when directed cycles exist
|-
| <code>break_cycles</code>
| <code>no</code>
| Drop edges that close directed cycles
|-
| <code>format</code>
| <code>mermaid</code>
| <code>mermaid</code> (render) or <code>raw</code> (source only, for debugging)
|}

'''Alias:''' <code><nowiki>{{#cargo_mermaid:…}}</nowiki></code> accepts the same parameters as <code><nowiki>{{#saintapedia_graph:…}}</nowiki></code>.

== Multiple Cargo tables ==

Two different features:

# '''One query, several tables''' — <code>tables=A,B</code> + <code>join on=…</code> (same rules as <code>#cargo_query</code>)
# '''Dual-table mode''' — <code>nodes_table</code> + <code>edges_table</code> (two queries; nodes keep their own Type/Country for <code>style_by</code> / <code>subgraph_by</code>)

=== Example: single-query join ===

<pre>
{{#saintapedia_graph:
tables=Grants,Organizations
|join on=Grants.Funder=Organizations._pageName
|fields=Grants.Funder,Grants.Recipient,Grants.Amount,Organizations.Type
|source_field=Funder
|target_field=Recipient
|edge_label=Amount
|direction=LR
|limit=300
}}
</pre>

In '''edge mode''', each row is one edge; node names come from source/target values. A join can enrich filters or labels.

For styled nodes that live in a different table from the edges, use '''dual-table mode''' (see Quick start) rather than a single join.

Not in this version: recursive multi-hop expansion (“everyone within 2 steps of X”).

== Templates ==

* <code><nowiki>{{Org chart|style=Type|subgraph=Country}}</nowiki></code> — hierarchy over Organizations
* <code><nowiki>{{Funding network|style=Type|subgraph=Country|edges_where=Year>=2023}}</nowiki></code> — dual-table Organizations + Grants

<code>style</code> / <code>subgraph</code> arguments must be real Cargo column names.

== Tips for good graphs ==

* Prefer '''Page'''-type fields for parent/funder/recipient so click links resolve
* Keep <code>limit=</code> reasonable (hundreds, not tens of thousands)
* Use <code>where=</code> / <code>edges_where=</code> to focus (year, type, program)
* <code>direction=TD</code> for org charts; <code>LR</code> for networks
* <code>format=raw</code> if a diagram fails — inspect Mermaid source
* Hard-refresh the browser after extension updates (Ctrl+Shift+R)
* Editor messages (errors, cycle/theme warnings) are English even if the wiki language is not

== Troubleshooting ==

{| class="wikitable"
! Symptom
! What to try
|-
| “tables parameter is required”
| Add <code>tables=YourTable</code>, or use both <code>nodes_table</code> and <code>edges_table</code>
|-
| Missing parent / edge fields
| Set <code>parent_field</code> '''or''' both <code>source_field</code> and <code>target_field</code> (not both modes at once)
|-
| Dual mode missing a table
| Both <code>nodes_table</code> and <code>edges_table</code> are required
|-
| No results
| Check Cargo data at [[Special:CargoTables]]; re-save pages that <code>#cargo_store</code>
|-
| Nodes and edges do not match
| In dual mode set <code>node_id=_pageName</code> so endpoints equal page titles
|-
| Unknown theme warning
| Use <code>default</code>, <code>base</code>, <code>dark</code>, <code>forest</code>, or <code>neutral</code>
|-
| Cycle warning
| Expected if the directed graph loops. Use <code>break_cycles=yes</code> to drop back-edges
|-
| “Diagram failed to render”
| Hard-refresh; try <code>format=raw</code>; check browser console
|-
| Too many expensive parser functions
| Fewer graphs per page (dual mode counts as two), or raise <code>$wgExpensiveParserFunctionLimit</code>
|-
| Join error from Cargo
| Ensure <code>join on=</code> mentions every table in <code>tables=</code>
|}

== Configuration (admins) ==

Common <code>LocalSettings.php</code> / Canasta settings:

<pre>
$wgSaintapediaGraphDefaultDirection = 'TD';
$wgSaintapediaGraphDefaultLimit = 500;
$wgSaintapediaGraphMaxLimit = 1000;
$wgSaintapediaGraphClickable = true;
$wgSaintapediaGraphDefaultTheme = 'default';
$wgSaintapediaGraphWarnCycles = true;
$wgSaintapediaGraphBreakCycles = false;
</pre>

UI strings are English-only. A non-English <code>$wgLanguageCode</code> still shows English errors and warnings.

Scripts are same-origin ResourceLoader (bundled Mermaid). No CDN is required. See the extension README for CSP notes.

